{
  "requirement": "[`Sources`](../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/sources/struct.Sources.html) supplies\nbuilt-in filesystem listing, reading, outlining, text search, and structural\nsearch. Construct it with the project directory:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse trust_but_verify::sources::Sources;\n\nlet sources = Sources::new(repository_root);\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject requires `Sources`, built with `Sources::new(repository_root)`, to supply built-in listing, reading, outlining, text search and structural search. The supplied tests cover each operation on the real filesystem provider.\n\n- **Construction:** `Sources::new(root.path())` is called in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]` and in `...#fn[built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope]`.\n- **Listing:** `list` is asserted on its returned paths. It includes `keep.txt`, `src/nested.txt` and `.visible`, and it excludes ignored files and `.git`.\n- **Reading:** `read` is asserted to succeed on `.gitignore` and to fail on ignored files and on `.git/config`.\n- **Outlining:** `parse` is asserted to fail on ignored files. In the structural test, `parse` is asserted to return the expected `fingerprint_scheme` (`plain-text-structural-v1` for the unknown file, `rust-structural-v1` for `visible.rs`). The outline item count for the plain-text file is also asserted.\n- **Text search:** `search_text` is asserted on match counts and completeness, with a regex pattern, with scopes, and with a scope error for `..`.\n- **Structural search:** `search_structure` is asserted on the match path, selector and excerpt. It is also asserted on limits and completeness, on scopes, on the unsupported-language error, on Python results, and on the scope error for `..`.\n- **Provider defaults:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot]` checks that the provider's read, list and parse primitives compose into these operations.\n\nI found no obligation in the text that lacks a test with an assertion. Finer behaviors such as scoping and ignore rules belong to the refining requirements that these tests also reference.",
  "references": "4d41003c77972a16520215e0fd1626c3ad65e439c7c88420a89dd4756ab62d31",
